{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Limb (a) of the baseline test is met on the trip_record: TRP-00202 carries an 'arrived' event at 2026-07-24T23:13:10+08:00, so the driver did mark arrival at this pickup point.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00202"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.arrived_at",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Limb (b) is met and POL-NS-02 is satisfied on its own terms: the GPS trace places the driver inside the 150 m AIRPORT arrival radius for this pickup pin, with 63 qualifying in-radius fixes whose reported accuracy passes the 25 m filter, the first of them at 23:12:45 -- before the 23:13:10 arrival event. POL-NS-02 states that where qualifying in-radius fixes exist the clause is satisfied and the dispute turns on dwell duration under POL-NS-01(c), which is exactly this case. Because the driver held position INSIDE the arrival radius rather than outside it, the wrong-entrance clause POL-NS-03 is not engaged.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00202", "EV-TRIP-00202"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01", "POL-NS-02", "POL-NS-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.qualifying_fix_count",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Limb (c) is met: the driver's longest qualifying in-geofence run lasted 620 seconds, running from the first qualifying fix at 23:12:45 to 23:23:05, against the 480 second minimum dwell for the AIRPORT zone class. That is a surplus of 140 seconds, not a shortfall, and the dwell is measured from the first qualifying fix as the clause requires, not from the 'arrived' event.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00202"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.duration_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Limb (d) is met: nothing in the trip_record shows a boarding event, and the trip was terminated by the driver at 23:23:20 on cancellation_reason_code RIDER_NO_SHOW -- fifteen seconds after the qualifying dwell ended at 23:23:05 and more than two minutes after the 480 second minimum elapsed on any computation of the clock. The code is one of the three the clause names (RIDER_NO_SHOW, RIDER_UNREACHABLE, EXCESSIVE_WAIT), and it is not DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00202"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.cancellation_reason_code",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-05 does not defeat the arrival marker: the 'arrived' event at 23:13:10 falls only 25 seconds after the in-radius run began at 23:12:45, so at the moment of the marker the driver was already stationary inside the geofence -- not more than 300 m from the pin and not travelling at 15 km/h or above. There is no false-arrival correction to make and no limb (i) or (ii) refund follows.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00202", "EV-TRIP-00202"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-05"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.dwell_start_offset_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-06 is not engaged: the effective in-geofence dwell of 620 seconds exceeds the 480 second AIRPORT minimum, so there is no shortfall and no refund follows from that clause. The accumulation limb (i) is in any event unavailable, because EV-ADVIS-00202-01 is MISSING (no payload, weight 0.0) and POL-NS-06(i) requires a traffic_advisory that is present and populated -- but the driver has no need of it, since this is a single continuous in-geofence interval that already clears the minimum on its own.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00202", "EV-ADVIS-00202-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.shortfall_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-04 cannot rescue the rider, because limb (a) fails on the face of the log: that limb requires a rider message during the waiting window whose content is locating or coordinating, and the chat_log for this trip contains no rider message at all. Disclosure of impairment: EV-CHAT-00202 is IMPAIRED, weight_multiplier 0.85, issue code UNREAD_MESSAGE. Its three entries are the system arrival notice at 23:13:11 and the driver's own two messages -- 23:14:02 'boss i'm at door 5 T3 arrival, black Toyota Altis SLA1234X' and 23:19:30 'boss? still waiting ah'. With limb (a) unmet, the clause does not apply regardless of the rider's account of a delayed flight, and the driver's two unanswered messages are consistent with the counterparty statement on file that he messaged twice with his plate number.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00202"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-04"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.85
    },
    {
      "text": "Rider presence is undecidable on this record and is neutral rather than adverse: all 88 rider fixes report 45 m to 80 m horizontal accuracy and are filtered out under the accuracy rule POL-NS-04(c) shares with POL-NS-02, leaving rider_qualifying_fix_count at 0. That neither satisfies nor fails limb (c) of POL-NS-04, and the artifact is down-weighted to that extent under POL-GEN-02. It does not help the rider either: because limb (a) already fails, POL-NS-04 is unavailable on either footing, and rider presence or absence is not the test once the dwell is met.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00202"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-04", "POL-GEN-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.rider_qualifying_fix_count",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The amount charged is the amount the schedule prescribes, so POL-NS-08(d) is not engaged: fee_schedule.resolution_rule takes the GREATER of the zone-class fee and the vehicle-tier fee -- SGD 6.00 for AIRPORT against SGD 4.00 for RYDE_X -- which is SGD 6.00, and fare_breakdown.cancellation_fee is exactly SGD 6.00 on a ledger whose payment_status is CHARGED with refund_issued_sgd 0.00.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00202", "EV-TRIP-00202"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01", "POL-NS-08"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.schedule_fee",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver is entitled to compensation under POL-NS-07 because POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full and no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces it: 80 percent of the SGD 6.00 fee is SGD 4.80, which is the driver_compensation figure the fare evidence itself computes. The anti-farming check, run only on the two fields the clause names, does not trip: driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 1, below the threshold of 4, and 1 divided by completed_trips_30d of 168 is about 0.006, far below 0.08. Disclosure of impairment: EV-DPROF-00202 is IMPAIRED, weight_multiplier 0.9, issue code SCHEMA_VERSION_MISMATCH; the counters sit an order of magnitude below both thresholds so the discount changes nothing. No lifetime counter such as prior_no_show_flags is relied on, per POL-GEN-01.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00202", "EV-FARE-00202"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-07", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.driver_compensation",
      "asserted_weight": 0.9
    },
    {
      "text": "No escalation trigger fires. The deciding fact -- the in-geofence dwell -- rests on EV-GPS-00202 at weight_multiplier 1.0, with 100 percent coverage, point_count 116, no gaps and max_gap_sec 0.0, so POL-NS-08(b) is not met; the trip_record arrived event reconciles with the trace well inside the 90 second tolerance of POL-NS-08(a); the chat_log holds exactly the 3 messages that trip_record.chat_message_count records and its longest inter-message gap (23:14:03 to 23:19:31) falls wholly after, and not across, the arrival marker, so POL-NS-08(c) is not met. EV-CHAT-00202 is down-weighted at 0.85 under POL-GEN-02 only and does not meet any limb of POL-NS-08, so POL-NS-09(e) does not apply. On the counters POL-NS-09(c) and (d) actually read, rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 1, below the threshold of 3, and rider_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d and driver_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d are both 0.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00202", "EV-TRIP-00202", "EV-CHAT-00202", "EV-RPROF-00202", "EV-DPROF-00202"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-08", "POL-NS-09", "POL-GEN-02"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The outcome the record produces is DRIVER_COMPENSATION with amount_sgd SGD 4.80, mirroring driver_compensation_sgd, while the SGD 6.00 fee stands as it presently is -- on this rider-filed dispute that is NO_ACTION on the fee, with payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd 0.00 left untouched. POL-GEN-03 makes the ruling value DRIVER_COMPENSATION precisely because the case produces a payment to the driver, and states that amount_sgd carries the same figure in that instance; the rider's request to waive the charge is not supported.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00202"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-03", "POL-NS-07"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.payment_status",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

