    "explanation": "To the rider and to the driver.\n\nThe SGD 6.00 no-show fee stands, and the platform pays the driver SGD 4.80 compensation.\n\nThe charge is valid. All four conditions of POL-NS-01 hold on this record. (a) The trip record carries a driver 'arrived' event at 23:13:10. (b) The GPS trace places the driver inside the 150 m AIRPORT arrival radius with 63 qualifying fixes at 25 m accuracy or better, the first at 23:12:45, before the arrived event, so POL-NS-02 is satisfied. (c) The driver held position continuously inside the geofence for 620 seconds (23:12:45 to 23:23:05), above the 480-second AIRPORT minimum, measured from the first qualifying fix as the clause requires. (d) There is no boarding event, and the driver terminated the trip at 23:23:20 on RIDER_NO_SHOW, after the required dwell elapsed — one of the three codes the clause names, and not DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE.\n\nNo clause displaces the charge. POL-NS-03 (wrong entrance) is not engaged: the driver held position inside the arrival radius, not outside it. POL-NS-04 (rider contact unanswered) requires as limb (a) that the rider sent a locating or coordinating message in the chat log; the log contains no rider message at all, so the clause is unavailable on either footing, and rider presence is not its test. POL-NS-05 (false arrival) is not engaged: at the 23:13:10 marker the driver was stationary inside the geofence, 25 seconds after the run began — not more than 300 m from the pin and not moving at 15 km/h or above — so there is nothing to correct and no limb (i) or (ii) refund follows. POL-NS-06 (shortfall) is not engaged: 620 seconds exceeds the 480-second minimum by 140 seconds. Because POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full and nothing in POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces it, POL-NS-07 governs.\n\nThe amount is right. Under fee_schedule.resolution_rule the fee is the GREATER of the AIRPORT zone-class fee (SGD 6.00) and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee (SGD 4.00), which is SGD 6.00; the ledger charges exactly SGD 6.00 with refund_issued_sgd 0.00, so POL-NS-08(d) is not engaged. Compensation is 80 per cent of SGD 6.00 = SGD 4.80, and the anti-farming check does not trip: driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 1, below 4, and 1 over 168 completed trips is about 0.006, far below 0.08. The ruling value is therefore DRIVER_COMPENSATION, with amount_sgd mirroring driver_compensation_sgd at SGD 4.80; on the fee itself the charge stands (NO_ACTION), and the rider's request to waive it is not supported.\n\nThe rider's presence is undecidable, and I do not hold that against him. All 88 rider fixes report 45 m to 80 m horizontal accuracy — what a handset inside a terminal reports — and are filtered out under the 25 m rule that POL-NS-04(c) shares with POL-NS-02, leaving rider_qualifying_fix_count at 0. Rider presence is therefore undecidable and neutral: the test could not be run, and the distances carried in derived.rider_presence, computed on those filtered fixes, place the rider nowhere at all. The rider's account that he did not see the messages until later is consistent with the chat log, in which the system arrival notice and both driver messages all carry read_at null. But rider presence is not the deciding fact: POL-NS-01 charges the fee on the driver's arrival and dwell, and POL-NS-06 states the outcome holds whether or not the rider was present.\n\nThe rider's escalation argument is rejected. The deciding fact — the qualifying in-geofence dwell — is carried by the GPS trace at weight 1.0 (100 per cent coverage, 116 fixes, no gaps, max_gap_sec 0.0) and the trip record at 1.0. POL-NS-08(b) is not met on those artifacts, so POL-NS-09(e) does not fire: no deciding fact rests solely on evidence impaired under limbs (a) to (d) of POL-NS-08. I accept the rider fixes are undecidable, but that does not impair the deciding fact and does not bar the ruling. No other POL-NS-09 trigger fires: confidence is above the 0.70 floor; no two admissible artifacts contradict each other on arrival, dwell or rider presence (the 23:13:10 arrived event and the 620-second dwell reconcile well inside the 90-second tolerance of POL-NS-08(a)); rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 1, below 3; and the anti-farming check does not trip.\n\nImpairments named, as POL-GEN-02 requires. EV-CHAT-00202 is IMPAIRED at weight 0.85 (issue UNREAD_MESSAGE): it explains why the rider saw nothing, but it does not carry the dwell and does not decide the case, so the discount does not change the result. EV-DPROF-00202 is IMPAIRED at weight 0.9 (issue SCHEMA_VERSION_MISMATCH): its anti-farming counters sit an order of magnitude below the POL-NS-07 thresholds, so the discount changes nothing. EV-ADVIS-00202-01 is MISSING at weight 0.0 and carries no fact; no accumulation under POL-NS-06(i) is needed because the dwell is a single continuous interval that already clears the minimum. Confidence is 0.9: the dwell rests on the GPS trace and trip record at weight 1.0, and taking the lowest weight among the artifacts the compensation ruling relies on — the driver profile at 0.9 — keeps it above the 0.70 escalation floor. Under POL-GEN-01 the driver's prior_no_show_flags is a lifetime counter and context only, and the driver correctly did not rely on it; I have not used it, nor the rider's rating, account age or trip counts, all of which are context only."
