    "explanation": "Both of you: this is about the SGD 6.00 no-show cancellation fee on trip TRP-00202 (Changi T3, AIRPORT zone class). The fee turns on the driver's arrival and waiting time, and that is proved.\n\nTo the rider. The charge does not depend on whether the delay was your fault or whether you read any message. The record shows the driver entered the 150 m AIRPORT pickup geofence at 23:12:45 and held position there continuously for 620 seconds, to 23:23:05 — above the 480-second minimum for an airport pickup — and then cancelled at 23:23:20 on reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW, with no boarding event. That satisfies POL-NS-01 on all four limbs. The arrival marker was not false under POL-NS-05: at the 23:13:10 marker the driver was stationary inside the geofence, only 25 seconds after the run began, so there is no recomputed clock and no refund. POL-NS-03 does not apply either, because the driver was inside the arrival radius, not outside it.\n\nI accept your central point about your own position. All 88 fixes in the rider track report 45–80 m accuracy and are ignored under the shared 25 m filter, so your location cannot be established one way or the other. POL-NS-04 makes that undecidable and neutral — it is not evidence that you were absent — and I have not read it against you. But it does not decide this case. POL-NS-01 does not require proof that you were absent, and POL-NS-04 cannot exonerate you because its limb (a) requires a locating or coordinating message from you during the wait, and you sent none. The chat entries (the system 'driver has arrived' notice at 23:13:11 and the driver's messages at 23:14:02 and 23:19:30) all carry read_at null, which is consistent with your account that you saw nothing until later; the driver's account of two messages with his plate number matches the log. None of this moves the fee, because the charge does not depend on whether the messages were read.\n\nI refuse the escalation you sought. POL-NS-09(e) applies only where the ONLY evidence for the deciding fact is impaired under POL-NS-08(a)–(d). The deciding fact here — the driver's in-geofence wait — is carried by EV-GPS-00202 at weight 1.0 (100% coverage, 116 fixes, no gaps, max gap 0 s) and by EV-TRIP-00202 at weight 1.0, with no clock skew (the 23:13:10 arrival event and the 23:23:20 termination both reconcile with the trace within seconds) and no chat defect. POL-NS-08(a)–(d) is not met. Your position is not the deciding fact, so its undecidability cannot trigger escalation. The one fact your track might have settled simply is not an element of the charge.\n\nTo the driver. You are entitled to compensation. The fee is correctly computed: the resolution rule takes the GREATER of the AIRPORT zone-class fee (SGD 6.00) and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee (SGD 4.00), i.e. SGD 6.00, which is exactly what the ledger charges, so there is no POL-NS-08(d) defect. POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full and no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces it, so POL-NS-07 pays you 80% of SGD 6.00 = SGD 4.80, the platform retaining the residual 20%. The anti-farming check, run only on the two fields the clause names (no_show_terminations_30d = 1, below the threshold of 4; 1 ÷ 168 completed trips ≈ 0.006, below 0.08), does not trip. Because a payment to the driver is the outcome, the ruling value is DRIVER_COMPENSATION and amount_sgd carries the same SGD 4.80 (POL-GEN-03); the SGD 6.00 fee stands as charged.\n\nImpairment and confidence. EV-CHAT-00202 is impaired (weight 0.85; issue UNREAD_MESSAGE); it is down-weighted under POL-GEN-02 only, and it does not meet POL-NS-08(c), since it holds exactly the 3 messages the trip record counts and its longest gap (23:14:03–23:19:31) falls after, not across, the arrival marker. EV-DPROF-00202 is impaired (weight 0.9; issue SCHEMA_VERSION_MISMATCH); it carries the anti-farming counters, and the discount changes nothing because those counters sit far below both thresholds. EV-ADVIS-00202-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0) and can carry no fact; the POL-NS-06(i) accumulation it would have supported was neither available nor needed, because a single continuous 620-second interval already clears the minimum. No context-only profile field was used as a ground: prior_no_show_flags appears only as a field expressly not relied on (POL-GEN-01). My confidence is capped at 0.9, the lowest weight among the artifacts carrying the facts this ruling rests on — the anti-farming clearance from the driver profile at 0.9, and the wait and arrival from the GPS trace and trip record at 1.0. That is above the 0.70 escalation floor, so no escalation arises on that ground either."
