{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "DRIVER_COMPENSATION",
    "amount_sgd": 4.8,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": 4.8,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To both parties: this dispute is decided on the record.\n\nThe SGD 6.00 cancellation fee is properly chargeable and stays as it is. For the charge to stand, the driver must have arrived at your pickup point and held position for the AIRPORT minimum of 480 seconds. The trip record carries the driver's 'arrived' marker at 23:13:10, and the GPS trace puts 63 fixes inside the 150 m Terminal 3 arrival radius, the first at 23:12:45 - before the marker - with unbroken coverage (116 fixes, no gaps, longest run 620 seconds, from 23:12:45 to 23:23:05). Measured from that first qualifying fix, as the clause requires, the dwell is 620 seconds against the 480-second minimum: a 140-second surplus, not a shortfall. The trip was then cancelled by the driver at 23:23:20 on RIDER_NO_SHOW. All four conditions of the baseline test are met, and none of the wrong-entrance (POL-NS-03), unanswered-contact (POL-NS-04), false-arrival (POL-NS-05) or shortfall (POL-NS-06) clauses displaces them. The amount is also correct: the resolution rule takes the greater of the AIRPORT zone-class fee (SGD 6.00) and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee (SGD 4.00), so SGD 6.00, and the fare breakdown reconciles exactly, so there is no fare defect.\n\nThe rider's argument for escalation is rejected. The rider's own position at the terminal cannot be established from the trace - all 88 rider fixes report 45-80 m accuracy and are filtered out under the 25 m rule - but that is undecidable and neutral, not adverse, and rider presence is not one of the conditions the fee depends on. The deciding fact, the driver's in-geofence dwell, rests on the driver's fixes in EV-GPS-00202 (unbroken, full weight) and on EV-TRIP-00202 (full weight); it is not carried by impaired evidence. The impaired-sole-evidence escalation condition therefore does not fire, and no other escalation trigger is met (confidence is above the 0.70 floor, no admissible artifacts contradict each other, no repeat-counterparty pattern, the anti-farming check does not trip). The rider's account that he did not see the messages is consistent with the record - the system notice and both driver messages all carry read_at null - but the contact clause fails independently because the log contains no rider message at all, and a rider's non-response does not by itself defeat a properly established dwell.\n\nDriver compensation: because the fee is properly chargeable, the driver is paid 80 percent of SGD 6.00, which is SGD 4.80. The anti-farming check reads only the two trailing-30-day counters; with 1 termination across 168 completed trips (ratio about 0.006) it is far below both thresholds, so compensation is paid. Two artifacts below full weight are named for completeness: EV-DPROF-00202 (weight 0.9, SCHEMA_VERSION_MISMATCH), which carries the anti-farming limb - its counters sit an order of magnitude below the thresholds, so the finding survives the discount and sets the confidence cap of 0.9; and EV-CHAT-00202 (weight 0.85, UNREAD_MESSAGE), which does not carry the deciding fact. The traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00202-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0) and carries no fact; it would matter only to a dwell-accumulation argument this single continuous 620-second interval does not need.\n\nOutcome: the ruling is DRIVER_COMPENSATION. The SGD 6.00 charge stands (no refund to the rider), and SGD 4.80 is paid to the driver; per the ruling vocabulary, amount_sgd mirrors driver_compensation_sgd at SGD 4.80, being the amount this ruling moves. No clause produces a referral."
